[hr]

[size=large][b]A better post editor[/b][/size]

The Editor Extras module upgrades SCEditor with a Bootstrap Icons toolbar, an emoji picker, GIF search (Tenor or GIPHY), tables, paste and drag-and-drop image upload, image resizing, @mentions and syntax-highlighted code.

[align=center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/amtekkie/mystudio/main/docs/screenshots/post-editor.png[/img][/align]

[hr]

[size=large][b]Profiles with personality[/b][/size]

Members can give their profile a banner: an uploaded image, a solid colour or a gradient. Profiles also show their latest posts.

[align=center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/amtekkie/mystudio/main/docs/screenshots/profile-banner.png[/img][/align]

[hr]

[size=large][b]For admins[/b][/size]

Pick an accent colour from nine presets or your own, upload a logo and favicon, and switch features on and off, all without touching code.

[align=center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/amtekkie/mystudio/main/docs/screenshots/acp-studio-settings.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/amtekkie/mystudio/main/docs/screenshots/acp-modules.png[/img][/align]

[hr]

[size=large][b]For theme developers[/b][/size]

The built-in editor runs on Monaco, the engine behind VS Code: a file tree, tabs, Emmet, and [b]Ctrl+S to save and update the forum in one step[/b].

[align=center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/amtekkie/mystudio/main/docs/screenshots/acp-theme-editor.png[/img][/align]

Prefer your own editor? Turn on auto-sync and the forum reloads itself a moment after you save.

[b]Built for AI coding assistants.[/b] Because a theme is just files with predictable names ([i]templates/header/header.html[/i] is the [i]header[/i] template), tools like Claude Code, Copilot and Cursor can find, edit and diff your theme like any other project. The repository even ships the context files they read first.

[b]Modules are plugins made simple.[/b] A folder, a [i]plugin.json[/i], an [i]init.php[/i] and an optional settings list. MyStudio builds the settings page and loads your CSS and JS for you:

[code]inc/plugins/mystudio/modules/my-module/
├── plugin.json
├── init.php
└── css/my-module.css[/code]

[hr]

[size=large][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]MyBB 1.8.38 or newer
[*]PHP 8.0+ with fileinfo, json and curl (the zip extension is now optional)
[*]MySQL 5.7+ or MariaDB 10.3+
[*]Apache 2.4+ or Nginx
[/list]

[size=large][b]Installing[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Upload [i]inc/plugins/ms.php[/i], [i]inc/plugins/mystudio/[/i], [i]admin/modules/mystudio/[/i], [i]jscripts/mystudio/[/i] and [i]themes/mystudio-default/[/i].
[*]Admin CP → Configuration → Plugins → [b]Install & Activate[/b] MyStudio.
[*]MyStudio → Manage Themes → Options → [b]Sync from Disk[/b], then [b]Set as Default[/b].
[/list]

[b]Upgrading from 2.0?[/b] Upload the new files over the old ones, then deactivate and re-activate MyStudio once so administrators receive the new MyStudio permissions.

